      "content": "From PPO to GRPO",
      "color": "black"
    },
    {
      "id": "t2",
      "type": "text",
      "bbox_2d": [38, 112, 1420, 150],
      "content": "Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) (Schulman et al., 2017) is an actor-critic RL algorithm that is widely used in the RL fine-tuning stage of LLMs (Ouyang et al., 2022). In particular, it optimizes LLMs by maximizing the following surrogate objective:",
      "color": "black"
    },
    {
      "id": "t3",
      "type": "math",
      "bbox_2d": [105, 245, 1403, 315],
      "content": "\\\\(J_{PPO}(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}[q \\sim P(Q), o \\sim \\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(O|q)] \\frac{1}{|o|} \\sum_{t=1}^{|o|} \\min \\left[ \\frac{\\pi_{\\theta}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}{\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(o_t|q, o_{<t})} A_t, \\text{clip} \\left( \\frac{\\pi_{\\theta}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}{\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}, 1-\\varepsilon, 1+\\varepsilon \\right) A_t \\right],",
      "color": "black"
    },
    {
      "id": "t4",
      "type": "text",
      "bbox_2d": [105, 360, 1420, 390],
      "content": "where \\(\\pi_{\\theta}\\) and \\(\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}\\) are the current and old policy models, and \\(q, o\\) are questions and outputs sampled from the question dataset and the old policy \\(\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}\\), respectively. \\(\\varepsilon\\) is a clipping-related hyper-parameter introduced in PPO for stabilizing training. \\(A_t\\) is the advantage, which is computed by applying Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE) (Schulman et al., 2015), based",
      "color": "black"
    }
  ]
}
